{"source_record_id": "sr_6d6a5d9e449d45d8bd04d463cd66e722", "source_row_uid": "sr_6d6a5d9e449d45d8bd04d463cd66e722", "source_id": "carcinogens_base", "drug": "O=S=O", "molecule_identity_key": "RAHZWNYVWXNFOC-UHFFFAOYSA-N", "bemis_murcko_scaffold": "", "Y": 0, "condition_atoms": ["route=inhalation", "species=rat"], "condition_group": "route=inhalation+species=rat", "condition_text": "", "pmid": "3371292", "study_id": "cited:laskin:1976", "label_method": "carcinogens_conditioned_source_votes.v2", "reviewer": "source_contract_with_stratified_codex_audit_not_human_expert", "raw_value": "negative", "molecule_name": "sulfur dioxide", "raw_record": {"paragraph_idx": 4, "support_text": "In Laskin's lifetime inhalation study of rats, no tumors were found in rats exposed only to SO₂, indicating that SO₂ alone was not carcinogenic in this experiment.", "agent_name": "sulfur dioxide", "agent_category": "individual_substance_or_drug", "carcinogenicity_conclusion": "negative", "evidence_basis": "animal_carcinogenicity_bioassay", "evidence_scope": "experimental_animal", "evidence_population_or_model": "rat", "cancer_or_tumor": null, "cancer_identifier": null, "carcinogenic_role": null, "classification_authority": null, "classification_label": null, "exposure_route": "inhalation", "qualifying_conditions": null, "extra_details": "From Laskin et al., 1976 lifetime exposure experiments.", "confidence": 0.75, "needs_more_context": false, "pmid": "3371292", "extraction_id": "ext_5", "SMILES": "O=S=O", "source_row_uid": "sr_6d6a5d9e449d45d8bd04d463cd66e722"}, "source_payload_sha256": "804c4928349dacf25ba5e2dd6ecda5fa26081cf8d4ff9ec8c3eb83e01c36aff3", "study_source_row_uids": ["sr_6d6a5d9e449d45d8bd04d463cd66e722"], "study_source_pmids": ["3371292"], "audit_id": "CF6"}
{"source_record_id": "sr_f0a8b4a384d84b3e83ceee0dad12fece", "source_row_uid": "sr_f0a8b4a384d84b3e83ceee0dad12fece", "source_id": "carcinogens_base", "drug": "C=CC[C@@H]1C(=O)N2C(N(C)C)=Nc3ccc(C)cc3N2C1=O", "molecule_identity_key": "WOIIIUDZSOLAIW-NSHDSACASA-N", "bemis_murcko_scaffold": "O=C1CC(=O)N2c3ccccc3N=CN12", "Y": 0, "condition_atoms": ["species=rat"], "condition_group": "species=rat", "condition_text": "", "pmid": "1261299", "study_id": "pmid:1261299", "label_method": "carcinogens_conditioned_source_votes.v2", "reviewer": "source_contract_with_stratified_codex_audit_not_human_expert", "raw_value": "negative", "molecule_name": "azapropazone", "raw_record": {"paragraph_idx": 27, "support_text": "In the carcinogenicity-testing section it is reported that preliminary work had established that azapropazone had only very slight bacteriostatic and cytostatic effects, and that the previous 54-week study in rats had revealed no evidence of carcinogenic activity for azapropazone. A newborn-mouse subcutaneous assay was also conducted (0.625 mg single subcutaneous dose to newborn mice; 253 animals studied) with 1% aqueous gelatin as negative controls and a 2% urethane solution as positive controls.", "agent_name": "azapropazone", "agent_category": "individual_substance_or_drug", "carcinogenicity_conclusion": "negative", "evidence_basis": "animal_carcinogenicity_bioassay", "evidence_scope": "experimental_animal", "evidence_population_or_model": "rat", "cancer_or_tumor": null, "cancer_identifier": null, "carcinogenic_role": null, "classification_authority": null, "classification_label": null, "exposure_route": null, "qualifying_conditions": null, "extra_details": "54-week study in rats; azapropazone described as having only very slight bacteriostatic and cytostatic effects. A separate newborn-mouse subcutaneous study (0.625 mg, up to 1.25 mg; 253 animals) was performed but no carcinogenicity result for azapropazone is reported in this passage.", "confidence": 0.9, "needs_more_context": false, "pmid": "1261299", "extraction_id": "ext_2", "SMILES": "C=CC[C@@H]1C(=O)N2C(N(C)C)=Nc3ccc(C)cc3N2C1=O", "source_row_uid": "sr_f0a8b4a384d84b3e83ceee0dad12fece"}, "source_payload_sha256": "0cf8c88c93e82d0618dae05927068c382f03897062d4b95ae46c399622b7d05e", "study_source_row_uids": ["sr_f0a8b4a384d84b3e83ceee0dad12fece"], "study_source_pmids": ["1261299"], "audit_id": "CF7"}
{"source_record_id": "sr_95ade97bb10a42fa94a7d07e1668c1d5", "source_row_uid": "sr_95ade97bb10a42fa94a7d07e1668c1d5", "source_id": "carcinogens_base", "drug": "O=C(O)COc1ccc(Cl)cc1Cl", "molecule_identity_key": "OVSKIKFHRZPJSS-UHFFFAOYSA-N", "bemis_murcko_scaffold": "c1ccccc1", "Y": 0, "condition_atoms": ["model=f344 rat", "route=oral", "species=rat"], "condition_group": "model=f344 rat+route=oral+species=rat", "condition_text": "", "pmid": "28303741", "study_id": "cited:jeffries:1995", "label_method": "carcinogens_conditioned_source_votes.v2", "reviewer": "source_contract_with_stratified_codex_audit_not_human_expert", "raw_value": "negative", "molecule_name": "2,4-Dichlorophenoxyacetic acid (2,4-D)", "raw_record": {"paragraph_idx": 180, "support_text": "Jeffries et al. 1995 was a guideline chronic toxicity/oncogenicity study in F344 rats dosed via the diet for 12 or 24 months with 2,4-D at 5, 75, or 150 mg/kg/day (96.45% purity). The reported findings included a decreased incidence of benign pituitary adenomas and decreased mammary gland hyperplasia, with no increase in tumors, consistent with a negative carcinogenicity result.", "agent_name": "2,4-Dichlorophenoxyacetic acid (2,4-D)", "agent_category": "individual_substance_or_drug", "carcinogenicity_conclusion": "negative", "evidence_basis": "animal_carcinogenicity_bioassay", "evidence_scope": "experimental_animal", "evidence_population_or_model": "F344 rat", "cancer_or_tumor": null, "cancer_identifier": null, "carcinogenic_role": null, "classification_authority": null, "classification_label": null, "exposure_route": "oral", "qualifying_conditions": null, "extra_details": "Dosing via diet for 12 or 24 months; doses 5, 75, 150 mg/kg/day; 96.45% purity; reported a decreased incidence of benign pituitary adenomas and decreased mammary gland hyperplasia (decreases, not increases); Klimisch score 1; doses ≥75 mg/kg/day exceed TSRC.", "confidence": 0.7, "needs_more_context": false, "pmid": "28303741", "extraction_id": "ext_1", "SMILES": "O=C(O)COc1ccc(Cl)cc1Cl", "source_row_uid": "sr_95ade97bb10a42fa94a7d07e1668c1d5"}, "source_payload_sha256": "0e5caf9eeac50eae4e05eb00900f5424c2b62907c5b5c014bd755df9645219a6", "study_source_row_uids": ["sr_95ade97bb10a42fa94a7d07e1668c1d5"], "study_source_pmids": ["28303741"], "audit_id": "CF8"}
{"source_record_id": "sr_fae6579f7bdd4b50894218980847c8a0", "source_row_uid": "sr_fae6579f7bdd4b50894218980847c8a0", "source_id": "carcinogens_base", "drug": "CN(N=O)C(=N)N[N+](=O)[O-]", "molecule_identity_key": "VZUNGTLZRAYYDE-UHFFFAOYSA-N", "bemis_murcko_scaffold": "", "Y": 1, "condition_atoms": ["species=rat"], "condition_group": "species=rat", "condition_text": "", "pmid": "9250888", "study_id": "pmid:9250888", "label_method": "carcinogens_conditioned_source_votes.v2", "reviewer": "source_contract_with_stratified_codex_audit_not_human_expert", "raw_value": "positive", "molecule_name": "MNNG (N-methyl-N'-nitro-N-nitrosoguanidine)", "raw_record": {"paragraph_idx": 55, "support_text": "We found that gastric carcinogenesis induced by MNNG was enhanced by combined treatment with ammonium acetate plus sodium hypochlorite and suppressed by supplementation with taurine, a scavenger of monochloramine. In the present study, all cancers were found in the antrum, where adenocarcinomas were defined as lesions in which neoplastic cells penetrated the muscularis mucosae to invade the submucosa or deeper layers.", "agent_name": "MNNG (N-methyl-N'-nitro-N-nitrosoguanidine)", "agent_category": "individual_substance_or_drug", "carcinogenicity_conclusion": "positive", "evidence_basis": "animal_carcinogenicity_bioassay", "evidence_scope": "experimental_animal", "evidence_population_or_model": "rat (Rattus norvegicus)", "cancer_or_tumor": "gastric adenocarcinoma (gastric cancer)", "cancer_identifier": "UMLS:C0278701", "carcinogenic_role": "general_or_unspecified_carcinogen", "classification_authority": null, "classification_label": null, "exposure_route": null, "qualifying_conditions": null, "extra_details": "Gastric carcinogenesis induced by MNNG was enhanced by combined treatment with ammonium acetate plus sodium hypochlorite and suppressed by taurine (monochloramine scavenger); all cancers arose in the antrum, not the fundus, despite elevated BrdU labeling in both regions.", "confidence": 0.9, "needs_more_context": false, "pmid": "9250888", "extraction_id": "ext_9", "SMILES": "CN(N=O)C(=N)N[N+](=O)[O-]", "source_row_uid": "sr_fae6579f7bdd4b50894218980847c8a0"}, "source_payload_sha256": "4be894f39ba11dc3331f42b9276cb9af7311b310f002f5db87727123cb7fd39c", "study_source_row_uids": ["sr_fae6579f7bdd4b50894218980847c8a0"], "study_source_pmids": ["9250888"], "audit_id": "CF9"}
{"source_record_id": "sr_cdeaa9154c304da3ad4fe927e262f545", "source_row_uid": "sr_cdeaa9154c304da3ad4fe927e262f545", "source_id": "carcinogens_base", "drug": "Cc1cccn2c1nc1ccc(N)nc12", "molecule_identity_key": "AYLURHVFAYRSHT-UHFFFAOYSA-N", "bemis_murcko_scaffold": "c1cnc2c(c1)nc1ccccn12", "Y": 1, "condition_atoms": ["model=f344 rat", "route=oral", "species=rat"], "condition_group": "model=f344 rat+route=oral+species=rat", "condition_text": "", "pmid": "6097472", "study_id": "pmid:6097472", "label_method": "carcinogens_conditioned_source_votes.v2", "reviewer": "source_contract_with_stratified_codex_audit_not_human_expert", "raw_value": "established", "molecule_name": "2-amino-6-methyldipyrido[1,2-a:3',2'-d]imidazole (Glu-P-1)", "raw_record": {"paragraph_idx": 0, "support_text": "Glu-P-1, isolated from a glutamic acid pyrolysate, was proved to be a multipotent carcinogen in rats, inducing intestinal tumors when administered orally to F344 rats. Intestinal tumors were produced for the first time in the series with heterocyclic amines, and were classified histologically as adenomas, adenocarcinomas, and mucinous carcinomas (mucinous carcinomas only in the small intestine).", "agent_name": "2-amino-6-methyldipyrido[1,2-a:3',2'-d]imidazole (Glu-P-1)", "agent_category": "individual_substance_or_drug", "carcinogenicity_conclusion": "established", "evidence_basis": "animal_carcinogenicity_bioassay", "evidence_scope": "experimental_animal", "evidence_population_or_model": "F344 rat", "cancer_or_tumor": "intestinal tumor", "cancer_identifier": "UMLS:C0021841", "carcinogenic_role": "general_or_unspecified_carcinogen", "classification_authority": null, "classification_label": null, "exposure_route": "oral", "qualifying_conditions": null, "extra_details": "Small intestine tumors were papillary, polypoid or umbilicated; large intestine tumors were commonly polypoid with a short stalk. Histology included adenomas, adenocarcinomas (some adjacent to adenomas), and mucinous carcinomas (small intestine only, endophytic growth with extensive mucus production). Tumor tissue transplanted subcutaneously into the flank grew within 3 months.", "confidence": 0.95, "needs_more_context": false, "pmid": "6097472", "extraction_id": "ext_2", "SMILES": "Cc1cccn2c1nc1ccc(N)nc12", "source_row_uid": "sr_cdeaa9154c304da3ad4fe927e262f545"}, "source_payload_sha256": "39315e7d49322a68b6fdfbe3c4cb7a7aa65ff115b0555456625aeb8b1f058d74", "study_source_row_uids": ["sr_cdeaa9154c304da3ad4fe927e262f545"], "study_source_pmids": ["6097472"], "audit_id": "CF10"}
{"source_record_id": "sr_b803db498c294a9cb260fd058d4188c4", "source_row_uid": "sr_b803db498c294a9cb260fd058d4188c4", "source_id": "carcinogens_base", "drug": "CCOC(N)=O", "molecule_identity_key": "JOYRKODLDBILNP-UHFFFAOYSA-N", "bemis_murcko_scaffold": "", "Y": 1, "condition_atoms": ["model=balb/c mouse", "route=injection_or_parenteral", "species=mouse"], "condition_group": "model=balb/c mouse+route=injection_or_parenteral+species=mouse", "condition_text": "", "pmid": "33000506", "study_id": "pmid:33000506", "label_method": "carcinogens_conditioned_source_votes.v2", "reviewer": "source_contract_with_stratified_codex_audit_not_human_expert", "raw_value": "positive", "molecule_name": "Urethane", "raw_record": {"paragraph_idx": 78, "support_text": "The paper reports that urethane induces TNF-α-mediated IDLA (induced lung adenocarcinoma) in mice, and confirmed that urethane induced lung inflammation and lung adenocarcinoma in BALB/c mice, with the tumor cells of AT-II cellular origin. Urethane was also used (injected i.p.) to induce IDLA over 6 months and to establish the pro-tumor inflammatory stage.", "agent_name": "Urethane", "agent_category": "individual_substance_or_drug", "carcinogenicity_conclusion": "positive", "evidence_basis": "animal_carcinogenicity_bioassay", "evidence_scope": "experimental_animal", "evidence_population_or_model": "BALB/c mice", "cancer_or_tumor": "lung adenocarcinoma (IDLA)", "cancer_identifier": "UMLS:C0152013", "carcinogenic_role": "general_or_unspecified_carcinogen", "classification_authority": null, "classification_label": null, "exposure_route": "injection_or_parenteral", "qualifying_conditions": null, "extra_details": "Urethane administered by intraperitoneal injection (e.g., once per week) induced TNF-α-mediated lung inflammation and lung adenocarcinoma in mice; used as an experimental tumor-induction model. Tumor cells of AT-II cellular origin (SP-C and TTF-1 positive).", "confidence": 0.75, "needs_more_context": false, "pmid": "33000506", "extraction_id": "ext_8", "SMILES": "CCOC(N)=O", "source_row_uid": "sr_b803db498c294a9cb260fd058d4188c4"}, "source_payload_sha256": "3ba979ba00191e8d2c7ac4abff16916ebe3d5bec508e47d4def9360cfb90a8f5", "study_source_row_uids": ["sr_b803db498c294a9cb260fd058d4188c4"], "study_source_pmids": ["33000506"], "audit_id": "CF11"}
{"source_record_id": "sr_7bb830ccc2614215ad453a3ed12ae4b8", "source_row_uid": "sr_7bb830ccc2614215ad453a3ed12ae4b8", "source_id": "carcinogens_base", "drug": "CNNC", "molecule_identity_key": "DIIIISSCIXVANO-UHFFFAOYSA-N", "bemis_murcko_scaffold": "", "Y": 1, "condition_atoms": ["route=injection_or_parenteral", "species=mouse"], "condition_group": "route=injection_or_parenteral+species=mouse", "condition_text": "", "pmid": "24971882", "study_id": "pmid:24971882", "label_method": "carcinogens_conditioned_source_votes.v2", "reviewer": "source_contract_with_stratified_codex_audit_not_human_expert", "raw_value": "positive", "molecule_name": "1,2-Dimethylhydrazine", "raw_record": {"paragraph_idx": 0, "support_text": "Colon cancer was induced in mice using 1,2-dimethylhydrazine (DMH, 20 mg/kg/week, s.c.) for fifteen weeks; examination of colonic tissue at the end of the experiment confirmed DMH-induced colon cancer in non-diabetic and diabetic mice, with metformin shown to protect against it.", "agent_name": "1,2-Dimethylhydrazine", "agent_category": "individual_substance_or_drug", "carcinogenicity_conclusion": "positive", "evidence_basis": "animal_carcinogenicity_bioassay", "evidence_scope": "experimental_animal", "evidence_population_or_model": "mouse (Mus musculus)", "cancer_or_tumor": "colon cancer", "cancer_identifier": "UMLS:C0007102", "carcinogenic_role": "general_or_unspecified_carcinogen", "classification_authority": null, "classification_label": null, "exposure_route": "injection_or_parenteral", "qualifying_conditions": null, "extra_details": "DMH was dosed subcutaneously at 20 mg/kg/week for fifteen weeks as the chemical colon carcinogen; metformin was evaluated for protective (chemopreventive) effects against this induction. Alias: DMH.", "confidence": 0.95, "needs_more_context": false, "pmid": "24971882", "extraction_id": "ext_1", "SMILES": "CNNC", "source_row_uid": "sr_7bb830ccc2614215ad453a3ed12ae4b8"}, "source_payload_sha256": "c99123e3e39501d933bc32bacdd85de014299b6c97e3909fab0c92a9efd4bc20", "study_source_row_uids": ["sr_7bb830ccc2614215ad453a3ed12ae4b8"], "study_source_pmids": ["24971882"], "audit_id": "CF12"}
{"source_record_id": "sr_59132e6fa38c4b79bd7fe719fa874328", "source_row_uid": "sr_59132e6fa38c4b79bd7fe719fa874328", "source_id": "carcinogens_base", "drug": "NC(=O)NCCN=O", "molecule_identity_key": "UQHIHGSVRWOEBF-UHFFFAOYSA-N", "bemis_murcko_scaffold": "", "Y": 1, "condition_atoms": ["species=mouse"], "condition_group": "species=mouse", "condition_text": "", "pmid": "10623665", "study_id": "pmid:10623665", "label_method": "carcinogens_conditioned_source_votes.v2", "reviewer": "source_contract_with_stratified_codex_audit_not_human_expert", "raw_value": "positive", "molecule_name": "nitrosoethylurea", "raw_record": {"paragraph_idx": 27, "support_text": "The text states that papillary tumors induced by nitrosoethylurea (ethyl nitrosourea) in mice were derived from alveolar type II cells, based on expression of SP-A but not CC-10. This reports induction of pulmonary papillary tumors by nitrosoethylurea in experimental mice.", "agent_name": "nitrosoethylurea", "agent_category": "individual_substance_or_drug", "carcinogenicity_conclusion": "positive", "evidence_basis": "animal_carcinogenicity_bioassay", "evidence_scope": "experimental_animal", "evidence_population_or_model": "mouse", "cancer_or_tumor": "pulmonary papillary tumor", "cancer_identifier": null, "carcinogenic_role": "general_or_unspecified_carcinogen", "classification_authority": null, "classification_label": null, "exposure_route": null, "qualifying_conditions": null, "extra_details": "Also called ethyl nitrosourea; cited work of Ward et al and Rehm et al.", "confidence": 0.85, "needs_more_context": false, "pmid": "10623665", "extraction_id": "ext_6", "SMILES": "NC(=O)NCCN=O", "source_row_uid": "sr_59132e6fa38c4b79bd7fe719fa874328"}, "source_payload_sha256": "6f945c05c60f1ce71866c9ce3d4cc72e7e037096fd13b8fe4425c5f262b0a885", "study_source_row_uids": ["sr_59132e6fa38c4b79bd7fe719fa874328"], "study_source_pmids": ["10623665"], "audit_id": "CF13"}
{"source_record_id": "sr_304f11d1f00044a39d907a83bc71b9f9", "source_row_uid": "sr_304f11d1f00044a39d907a83bc71b9f9", "source_id": "carcinogens_base", "drug": "c1ccc2c(c1)cc1ccc3cccc4ccc2c1c34", "molecule_identity_key": "FMMWHPNWAFZXNH-UHFFFAOYSA-N", "bemis_murcko_scaffold": "c1ccc2c(c1)cc1ccc3cccc4ccc2c1c34", "Y": 1, "condition_atoms": ["route=oral", "species=mouse"], "condition_group": "route=oral+species=mouse", "condition_text": "", "pmid": "1852928", "study_id": "cited:neal:1967", "label_method": "carcinogens_conditioned_source_votes.v2", "reviewer": "source_contract_with_stratified_codex_audit_not_human_expert", "raw_value": "positive", "molecule_name": "Benzo[a]pyrene", "raw_record": {"paragraph_idx": 20, "support_text": "Feeding BaP to mice produced gastric tumors (papillomas or carcinomas) with a dose-response; tumor incidences rose from 0/289 (controls) to 66/73 at 250 ppm, and a chi-square test gave P<0.001 for a significant association between gastric tumor incidence and BaP dose (adapted from Neal and Rigdon, 1967).", "agent_name": "Benzo[a]pyrene", "agent_category": "individual_substance_or_drug", "carcinogenicity_conclusion": "positive", "evidence_basis": "animal_carcinogenicity_bioassay", "evidence_scope": "experimental_animal", "evidence_population_or_model": "mouse", "cancer_or_tumor": "gastric tumors (papillomas or carcinomas)", "cancer_identifier": null, "carcinogenic_role": "general_or_unspecified_carcinogen", "classification_authority": null, "classification_label": null, "exposure_route": "oral", "qualifying_conditions": null, "extra_details": "Dose-response from 0 to 250 ppm; e.g., 24/34 at 50 ppm, 19/23 at 100 ppm, 66/73 at 250 ppm (Neal and Rigdon, 1967).", "confidence": 0.9, "needs_more_context": false, "pmid": "1852928", "extraction_id": "ext_14", "SMILES": "c1ccc2c(c1)cc1ccc3cccc4ccc2c1c34", "source_row_uid": "sr_304f11d1f00044a39d907a83bc71b9f9"}, "source_payload_sha256": "1cf71058a4427598949cb087b38a43de4f35ea6c740daacb45402f0013465685", "study_source_row_uids": ["sr_304f11d1f00044a39d907a83bc71b9f9"], "study_source_pmids": ["1852928"], "audit_id": "CF14"}
{"source_record_id": "sr_b2c39b5ce45e48e8a998c944e373594b", "source_row_uid": "sr_b2c39b5ce45e48e8a998c944e373594b", "source_id": "carcinogens_base", "drug": "CCN(N=O)C(N)=O", "molecule_identity_key": "FUSGACRLAFQQRL-UHFFFAOYSA-N", "bemis_murcko_scaffold": "", "Y": 1, "condition_atoms": ["species=rat"], "condition_group": "species=rat", "condition_text": "", "pmid": "16651633", "study_id": "pmid:16651633", "label_method": "carcinogens_conditioned_source_votes.v2", "reviewer": "source_contract_with_stratified_codex_audit_not_human_expert", "raw_value": "positive", "molecule_name": "N-ethyl-N-nitrosourea", "raw_record": {"paragraph_idx": 58, "support_text": "Rats were imaged beginning at 150 days of age to detect small lesions in a model of ENU (N-ethyl-N-nitrosourea)-induced gliomas, but tumors could not be visualized by MRI until they had reached at least 2 mm in diameter; this is consistent with an earlier report that ENU-induced gliomas below this size cannot be visualized.", "agent_name": "N-ethyl-N-nitrosourea", "agent_category": "individual_substance_or_drug", "carcinogenicity_conclusion": "positive", "evidence_basis": "animal_carcinogenicity_bioassay", "evidence_scope": "experimental_animal", "evidence_population_or_model": "rat", "cancer_or_tumor": "glioma", "cancer_identifier": "UMLS:C0017638", "carcinogenic_role": "general_or_unspecified_carcinogen", "classification_authority": null, "classification_label": null, "exposure_route": null, "qualifying_conditions": null, "extra_details": "ENU-induced gliomas used as an experimental model; by 150 days small lesions are expected but MRI cannot reliably visualize tumors smaller than about 2 mm diameter even with heavily T2-weighted sequences.", "confidence": 0.75, "needs_more_context": false, "pmid": "16651633", "extraction_id": "ext_6", "SMILES": "CCN(N=O)C(N)=O", "source_row_uid": "sr_b2c39b5ce45e48e8a998c944e373594b"}, "source_payload_sha256": "a846e618d53d77e23e947ab5d831a8f7c8d0d0df5381df486b595b2147b793a5", 